// @no-instantiate
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: an un-annotated local ALIASING an un-annotated object literal, returned
// from an un-annotated function. Seven lines. No import, no generic, no union, no twin, no
// annotation — and no type declaration at all, which is what makes it the smallest member of
// this class the tree has held. `vl check` exits 0 with NO diagnostics and is the ONLY command
// that misses it; `vl check --codegen` exits 1, `vl build` writes the `.wasm` and exits 1,
// `vl run` exits 1:
//
//   the emitted module is not valid wasm … type mismatch: expected i32, found (ref $type)
//
// (No byte offset quoted on purpose: it moves with the seed. The message is the stable
// identifier — note its DIRECTION, `expected i32`, which is the tell that the result valtype
// fell to the scalar default while the body hands back a ref.)
//
// THE ALIAS IS THE WHOLE OF IT. Controls, each ONE line different from this file, each RUN:
//   · `return c` — drop the intermediate local            → runs, prints 7
//   · `function mk(n: i32): Circle` with `type Circle = { r: i32 }` declared → runs, prints 7
//   · `return o.r` — the object never crosses the return  → runs, prints 7
//
// It is `silent-class-inventory.md` D41, and it is NOT a regression: byte-identical on
// `f2064bec`, same offset and same message.
//
// HOW IT WAS FOUND IS THE REUSABLE PART, and it is recorded in `std/array.vl`'s ledger as that
// file's twentieth entry. The D36/D38 retirement crossed a 900-cell grid before writing a word
// — and `type Sq` / `type Shape` are declared in every one of those 900 files, so the union was
// a CONSTANT in the population rather than an axis. A cell whose finding is "the union is not
// required" was outside it by construction, and this is that cell. The std review of the
// retirement found it, and its first diagnosis ("the route is the whole of it — D35's property
// at the RESULT position") was drawn from a direct-call control that still had the union
// declared and was therefore LOUD. Deleting the union makes the direct call silent too. Both
// halves matter: a MEASUREMENT catches the claim, a REVIEW catches the claim's edges.
//
// WHEN IT IS FIXED this file starts failing (the module instantiates): delete it, graduate a
// `@run` row, and read the note in `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` before touching
// `INVALID_MODULE_SRC`, which points at D39 rather than at this row.
function mk(n: i32) {
  const c = { r: n }
  const o = c
  return o
}

print(mk(7).r)
